  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Setting up a modern technical distribution and training centre in Bosnia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildkamp B.V., daughter company of applicant Jarola Holding B.V., is a technical wholesale company with 45 affiliates and a state-of-the-art distribution centre in Coevorden, with just-in-time deliveries to customers all around the Netherlands. In 2004 Wildkamp B.V. set up a Bosnian daughter company (Wiltehnik) for the coordination of purchasing products from 27 Bosnian SME producers.Together with two Bosnian suppliers, local partner Plamingo doo and partner Kovan M.I., Wildkamp B.V. wants to improve the output, knowledge and production efficiency of the other 25 Bosnian SMEs, supplying Wildkamp B.V.. They want to do this by setting up a joint venture for a local distribution and trainings centre in Sarajevo.All 25 SMEs will be upgraded by intensive training. Besides the joint venture itself, at least 4 companies will be certified ISO 9001 and Eco-label, within the scope of this project. Others will follow in the years thereafter. Besides the distribution and training centre, the joint venture will also set up and run a production line for the production of 650,000 compression fittings per year, which will be located in Plamingo&apos;s production hall for plastic products in Gracanica. Wildkamp B.V. currently imports these compression fittings from Germany.The distribution and training centre should result in better organisation, logistics and product quality from the Bosnian SMEs, which would increase their chances both on the local market, as well as for supplying more and better products to Wildkamp B.V.. The project will introduce Dutch knowledge on logistics and distribution to the sector in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</narrative>
  </description>
